// Generated from reviewed wiki-source Markdown. Do not edit by hand.
export const wikiPages = [{"title":"Beta Status","href":"wiki/Beta-Status.html","text":"  Beta Status\r\n\r\nThe public Roblox beta is being prepared. A native Studio Save to File and independent reopen have source, root, service-property and Terrain-voxel parity evidence for the selected development scene. Selected local Play input reached plot Claim, Build, starter construction and some farm, factory, animal and amenity routes.\r\n\r\nThe beta is not called published or verified until a specific Roblox place version passes a fresh public join, responsive controls, durable leave and rejoin, and account-isolation acceptance. The 56 earned building and rotation routes and the concurrent 14-building arrangement also remain open. No play link appears on the website as a finished beta while that proof is absent.\r\n\r\nThe public  development gallery  https://ding-ding-projects.github.io/roblox-farm-tycoon-gallery/  contains reviewed captures. A gallery image proves only the scene and version recorded with it, not a live-server release.\r\n"},{"title":"Buildings and Production","href":"wiki/Buildings-and-Production.html","text":"  Buildings and Production\r\n\r\nThe 14 construction definitions are silo, barn, personal market, supplies shop, restaurant, depot, hotel, restroom, feedmill, bakery, dairy, sugar mill, loom and preserves workshop. Every construction card in the  live guide  https://ding-ding-projects.github.io/roblox-farm-tycoon-guide/ guide  gives its level, exact coin and material cost, current timer and role. The free silo, wheat-funded barn and feedmill have selected local Play routes. A complete 14-building concurrent layout and all earned rotations remain unverified.\r\n\r\nThe feedmill makes four kinds of animal feed. The bakery makes bread, carrot cake and truffle tart; the dairy makes butter and cheese; the sugar mill makes sugar; the loom makes wool cloth; the preserves workshop makes strawberry jam and apple preserves. Each of the 13 recipe cards lists the input quantity, output quantity, station, level and current timer. Definitions are separate from published production proof.\r\n\r\nThe four upgrade definitions are barn capacity, silo capacity, production queue and land. The current land rule increases the animal placement allowance by one per tier, subject to a cap of 16; it does not increase the construction limit. The guide records each maximum tier, cost formula and capacity effect. A recipe's listed unlock level can precede the level needed to grow an ingredient or build its station: chicken feed lists level 1 but self-grown corn requires level 2, and butter lists level 6 but the owned dairy requires level 8. Purchases are server-authoritative; an incomplete request or unavailable saved profile must not be shown as a successful upgrade.\r\n"},{"title":"Crops and Items","href":"wiki/Crops-and-Items.html","text":"  Crops and Items\r\n\r\nThe source defines seven planting routes: wheat, corn, carrot, soybean, sugarcane, strawberry and apple saplings. Each crop consumes one seed or sapling, has a level requirement and timer, and returns its listed yield plus XP and one planting supply if storage permits. Wheat has selected native harvest evidence. Other crop routes remain in development until their full earned and published paths are proved.\r\n\r\nThe item catalogue contains 31 named goods: seven planting supplies, seven harvested crops, four animal products, four feeds and nine made goods. Values on the  live guide  https://ding-ding-projects.github.io/roblox-farm-tycoon-guide/ guide  come from a source snapshot, not a promise that a public sale or order is currently available. Its search can locate every individual item and show how it is obtained and used.\r\n\r\nThe animals are chicken, cow, sheep and pig. Each requires its matching feed and has a collection timer and product. The chicken has selected local purchase, feeding and collection evidence; the others need full earned and live acceptance. See  Buildings and Production  Buildings-and-Production.md .\r\n"},{"title":"Getting Started","href":"wiki/Getting-Started.html","text":"  Getting Started\r\n\r\nChoose a plot, use the owned management board to place starter soil, plant a seed, wait for its current timer, and harvest. Starter soil is free. Owned objects can be rearranged without an extra placement charge, while a new building uses earned materials, coins, its level unlock, and a construction timer.\r\n\r\nWheat is the first crop. Its current timer is five seconds under compact pacing, and one harvest yields three wheat and five XP when storage has room. Three wheat and 40 coins pay for the first barn. Five wheat and 70 coins pay for a feedmill. A free silo has a 30-second legacy timer, compacted to five seconds. The actual entry and interaction paths have only selected local Studio evidence, so published-server behavior must still be checked.\r\n\r\nThe  live guide  https://ding-ding-projects.github.io/roblox-farm-tycoon-guide/ guide  lists each cost, unlock, timer, product and evidence status. See  Crops and Items  Crops-and-Items.md  and  Buildings and Production  Buildings-and-Production.md .\r\n"},{"title":"Farm Tycoon Field Guide","href":"wiki/Home.html","text":"  Farm Tycoon Field Guide\r\n\r\nThe  live field guide  https://ding-ding-projects.github.io/roblox-farm-tycoon-guide/  has a searchable explanation of every defined crop, seed, item, animal, recipe, building, and upgrade. It also carries the  world lore  https://ding-ding-projects.github.io/roblox-farm-tycoon-guide/ lore  and current beta status. This wiki provides stable reference pages and maintenance notes. The website is documentation, not a playable version of Farm Tycoon.\r\n\r\n-  Getting Started  Getting-Started.md \r\n-  Crops and Items  Crops-and-Items.md \r\n-  Buildings and Production  Buildings-and-Production.md \r\n-  World Lore  World-Lore.md \r\n-  Beta Status  Beta-Status.md \r\n\r\n  Evidence language:   \"Observed locally\" means a selected route was actually exercised in Studio. \"In development\" means a definition exists but the full route is unverified. Neither label means that public-server behavior has passed.\r\n"},{"title":"World Lore","href":"wiki/World-Lore.html","text":"  World Lore\r\n\r\nThe valley began with a shared arrival hall and empty fields. New farmers chose a plot, placed the first soil, and learned what the land returned when they gave it time.\r\n\r\nWheat paid for the first barn. The barn sheltered animals; the feedmill gave those animals a daily rhythm. The depot, market, bakery, and later workshops grew around the same idea: the town becomes real when its people can use the doors, work the machines, and bring something home.\r\n\r\nOlder equipment remains in the depot because its makers left practical lessons behind. Every shutter, counter, and room should have a purpose. Ordinary harvests and careful construction shape the town's story.\r\n\r\nThis is original setting fiction for the public guide. It does not claim that unfinished quests, characters, or buildings are already playable. Read the  complete lore section on the website  https://ding-ding-projects.github.io/roblox-farm-tycoon-guide/ lore .\r\n"}];
